dth=\"20\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"6\" width=\"12\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"6\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"6\" width=\"6\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"7\" width=\"10\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"7\" width=\"6\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"16\" y=\"7\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"8\" width=\"10\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"8\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"11\" y=\"8\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffe771\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"8\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"16\" y=\"8\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"9\" width=\"9\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"11\" y=\"9\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffe771\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"9\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffe771\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"17\" y=\"9\" width=\"3\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"10\" width=\"9\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"9\" y=\"10\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"11\" y=\"10\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffe771\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"10\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"10\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffe771\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"10\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"17\" y=\"10\" width=\"3\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"11\" width=\"10\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"11\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"11\" y=\"11\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#ffe771\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"11\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"16\" y=\"11\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"12\" width=\"10\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"6\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"16\" y=\"12\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"13\" width=\"12\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"13\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#2c3882\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"13\" width=\"6\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"14\" width=\"20\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"15\" width=\"20\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"16\" width=\"20\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"17\" width=\"20\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"18\" width=\"20\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"19\" width=\"20\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#141c61\"/></svg><div><small>star5: 17 ticks round</small></div></div></figure><ul><li><b>Starting points.</b> Each loop has four blocks, and any of them can be laid in the map: <b>star2.3</b> begins on its last frame, so two stars of the same loop can still be a step apart.</li><li><b>Laying them.</b> Stars are placed on the sky blocks one at a time with a rule: never in the cell next to another star, and never the same loop as a star within four blocks. The sky repeats, but nothing near anything else blinks with it.</li><li><b>In the air.</b> Star blocks pull down like the sky, so Rima falls through them when he jumps.</li><li><b>The signs.</b> They are ordinary blocks with words in their pictures, set on the meadow.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "head": "Level 2: A Night Sky",
      "html": "<h1>Level 2: A Night Sky</h1><p>A bigger meadow under the second sky, with a moon and two low hills behind you. <b>THE SKY REPEATS, BUT NOTHING BLINKS IN STEP</b> stands at the start. <b>NEIGHBORS NEVER SHARE A LOOP</b> stands in the middle of the meadow. The door is past the moon.</p><p>There is nothing to collect. Look up as you walk, and stop under the stars for a moment.</p>"
    },
    {
      "head": "How this level is made",
      "html": "<h1>How level 2 is made</h1><ul><li><b>The sky.</b> The same six loops as in level 1, laid with the same rule. Open <b>two.map</b> and look at the sky: each star is a block such as <b>star3.1</b>, and no two of the same number are within four blocks of each other.</li><li><b>The moon.</b> It is nine blocks, <b>moon.00</b> to <b>moon.22</b>, one picture of a pale moon with a soft glow cut into a three by three square. Blocks are only 20 pixels, so a big thing is a square of them laid side by side. The moon never changes, so it has no loop.</li><li><b>The hills.</b> Three blocks wide and one high, <b>hill.0</b> to <b>hill.2</b>, a dark mound against the sky. They are in the air, like the stars, so Rima walks in front of them.</li><li><b>The night.</b> The palette's sky ramp is dark blue, and the grass and dirt ramps are darker than in a day game. Nothing else changes: the same blocks, in a night palette (<b>twin.pal</b>).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "head": "What it cannot do",
      "html": "<h1>What it cannot do</h1><p>These are the engine's limits, so you can plan around them.</p><ul><li><b>It cannot give each cell its own clock.</b> The clock belongs to the block number, so every cell of one block changes in the same tick. Stars that do not blink together need different blocks.</li><li><b>It has no random.</b> There is no random timer and no random block. The sky only feels random: the same blocks, laid by a rule, repeating from the first tick.</li><li><b>It cannot fade.</b> A block only turns into another block, so a star's brightness is as smooth as the frames you draw. Each frame is a block of your 150, and each loop costs four, so six loops cost 24.</li><li><b>It cannot keep the loops apart for ever.</b> Loops with different times drift in and out of step. With 23 and 37 ticks they meet only every 851 ticks (about 47 seconds), and then only for a moment.</li><li><b>Every loop starts together.</b> When a level begins, every loop is at its first frame and every first change is its own time away, so the sky settles into its pattern after a few seconds.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "head": "Make it yours",
      "html": "<h1>Make it yours</h1><p>Try one change at a time, and play after each:</p><ul><li>In <b>one.bbl</b>, change the <b>Time</b> of <b>sync0.0</b> to 5 and watch one star blink out of step.</li><li>Change the <b>Time</b> of the dim frame of one loop from 16 to 40 and watch a lazier star.</li><li>Draw a shooting star: a loop of four frames that moves the star across the block.</li><li>Lay <b>star2.0</b> next to <b>star2.0</b> in <b>two.map</b> and see how clearly two matching stars show.</li><li>Draw a lighthouse lamp that turns on and off in its own loop.</li></ul><p>The home page's <b>Starters</b> tab has more small games like this one.</p>"
    }
  ]
}
